<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech fund BOHATSTVI CZK 674 mln 1996 net loss.</title>
<headline>Czech fund BOHATSTVI CZK 674 mln 1996 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audited results for year ending</p>
<p>December 31, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net result	   674.159 loss    vs     30.808 profit</p>
<p> Operational result	77.570 loss    vs     44.851 loss</p>
<p> Total assets	   3,091.559	   vs  2,691.465</p>
<p> Financial investment 1,395.633	   vs  1,011.185</p>
<p> Current assets	 1,622.496	   vs  1,699.567</p>
<p> Short-term loans	 188.482	   vs    510.424</p>
<p> Financial holdings   1,434.014	   vs  1,159.143</p>
<p> Basic capital	  1,255.527	   vs  1,255.527</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is a.s. IF Bohatstvi, a closed-end investment fund. It is managed by PIAS a.s., the investment arm of bank IPB a.s..</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
